# Docs index frontmatter

`plugins/llms-txt.js` builds `/api/v1/index.json` from page frontmatter. Quilr Assist (the help chat in the admin console) uses it to pick the page that answers an admin's question. See CLAUDE.md rule 9.

## Every new page

```yaml
description: "One sentence on what the page covers."
```

## Pages that document a console screen

Required for new pages under `docs/console/` (except `get-started/` and `legacy-v1/`). Add them in other products too when a page documents one whole console screen (for example the LLM Gateway settings page).

```yaml
console_path: /settings/organization/audit-logs     # or a list: [/policy, /policy/engine]
aliases: [audit logs, audit trail]
```

- `console_path`: the exact route from quilr-console `frontend/src/lib/appPaths.ts`. Static routes only, never parameterised ones. Never two pages for the same route. It can be empty (`console_path: []`) when the page documents no single screen (a workflow or concept page); under `docs/console/` the key must still be present.
- `aliases`: words admins use for the screen or feature, including old names. Quote numbers (`"429"`).

## Rules

- Keep `console_path` and `aliases` when a page is moved, renamed or split.
- Enforced on new pages by `.husky/pre-commit` (`node scripts/check-doc-frontmatter.js --staged`). Check a draft with `node scripts/check-doc-frontmatter.js <file>`. `npm run check-frontmatter` lists what existing pages are missing.
- A bad `console_path` or `aliases` value also fails `npm run build`.
